  publishDate="2026-03-28"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>

<p>A white-label audit tool removes or replaces vendor branding in a client-facing output. Before subscribing, decide whether you need a branded PDF, editable template, scheduled delivery, client portal or custom domain. Vendors use “white label” for different combinations of these features.</p>

<h2 id="what-is-white-label-auditing">What Is White-Label Auditing?</h2>

<p>White labelling changes presentation; it does not turn an automated issue list into an expert audit. Your deliverable should still state the scope, evidence, priority, owner, recommended action and validation method. It should also disclose material limitations, including pages or states the crawler could not access.</p>

<h2 id="top-tools">Tools to Shortlist</h2>

<p><a href="https://seranking.com/white-label.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">SE Ranking</a> documents branded platform and reporting options. <a href="https://www.woorank.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">WooRank</a> documents custom report templates and white-label reports for agency sales workflows. <a href="https://www.semrush.com/kb/34-my-reports" rel="noopener noreferrer">Semrush My Reports</a> documents report creation and scheduling; check its current branding entitlement for the plan or add-on under consideration.</p>

<p>A crawler with strong exports can also feed an independently branded report. This is useful when analysts need to combine crawl evidence with Search Console, analytics, accessibility and manual findings.</p>

<h2 id="feature-comparison">Feature Comparison</h2>

<div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="White-label audit tool acceptance criteria">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Test before purchase</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Branding</td><td>Export a sample and inspect the cover, headers, footers, URLs, email sender and vendor marks.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Editing</td><td>Confirm whether you can remove irrelevant checks and add analysis, owners and due dates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Evidence</td><td>Open a reported issue and export every affected URL with the observed field.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Delivery</td><td>Test scheduled email, portal access, permissions and expiry with a non-admin account.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>History</td><td>Verify how fixed, new and recurring issues appear between comparable crawls.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><small>Swipe or scroll horizontally to view the full table on smaller screens.</small></p>

<h2 id="branded-reports">Build a Useful Branded Report</h2>

<p>Lead with the decision the client needs to make. Group findings by outcome or owning team, not by the vendor's menu. Link each recommendation to reproducible evidence and separate confirmed defects from opportunities that need further research. Our <a href="/seo-website-audit/report/">audit report guide</a> and <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">example report</a> show the expected structure.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">Check Current Entitlements</h2>

<p>Prices and feature bundles change. On the date you buy, record the official plan, billing term, included seats, project and page limits, report allowance, portal entitlement, custom-domain support, API access and cancellation terms. Ask the vendor to confirm any feature that is central to the contract.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-sell-audits">Scope the Audit Before Selling It</h2>

<p>Define the site or properties covered, crawl and manual checks, exclusions, deliverable format, number of review calls and whether implementation is included. Price the analyst time required to verify and prioritise findings; automated report generation is only one part of the work.</p>

<p><small>Vendor capabilities checked against official product documentation on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

